{"title":"Career Roadmap: Sustainability Executive","role":"Sustainability Executive","summary":"A Sustainability Executive supports organizations in reducing environmental impact, improving resource efficiency, implementing sustainability initiatives, collecting ESG data and communicating sustainability performance.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Environmental Studies / Ecology"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in sustainability, environmental management, ESG, climate action, resource efficiency, reporting, stakeholder engagement and sustainability analytics"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Sustainability Executive supports organizations in reducing environmental impact, improving resource efficiency, implementing sustainability initiatives, collecting ESG data and communicating sustainability performance."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sustainability programme coordination"},{"text":"Environmental data collection"},{"text":"ESG reporting support"},{"text":"Carbon/emissions data"},{"text":"Energy and water monitoring"},{"text":"Waste management"},{"text":"Resource efficiency"},{"text":"Sustainability audits"},{"text":"Environmental awareness"},{"text":"Stakeholder engagement"},{"text":"Sustainable procurement awareness"},{"text":"Climate-risk analysis"},{"text":"Sustainability communication"},{"text":"CSR/environmental projects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Environmental Studies/Ecology provides a strong foundation, but technical environmental roles such as environmental engineering, laboratory analysis, certain EHS positions or regulated environmental consultancy may require specialized science/engineering qualifications."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Environmental foundation"},{"text":"Ecology, environmental science, sustainability"},{"text":"Environmental assessment"},{"text":"Only theoretical knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Sustainability management"},{"text":"Climate, energy, waste, water, environmental policy"},{"text":"Sustainability project"},{"text":"No quantitative skills"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"ESG & sustainability analytics"},{"text":"ESG, carbon accounting, reporting, Excel/Power BI"},{"text":"ESG dashboard/report"},{"text":"Treating ESG as only CSR"}],[{"text":"Final stage"},{"text":"Professional sustainability practice"},{"text":"Reporting, audits, climate strategy, internship"},{"text":"Sustainability portfolio + internship"},{"text":"No real organizational/project exposure"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1 — Environmental Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ecology"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Biodiversity"},{"text":"Ecosystems"},{"text":"Natural resources"},{"text":"Environmental pollution"},{"text":"Climate fundamentals"},{"text":"Environmental economics"},{"text":"Environmental ethics"},{"text":"Research methodology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Local ecosystem study"},{"text":"Environmental issue report"},{"text":"Biodiversity documentation project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2 — Sustainability Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sustainable development"},{"text":"Circular economy"},{"text":"Resource efficiency"},{"text":"Water management"},{"text":"Waste management"},{"text":"Renewable energy"},{"text":"Sustainable consumption"},{"text":"Environmental policy"},{"text":"Environmental impact"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the three broad dimensions:"},{"type":"flow","